content='''<section class="pi-objective sr-intro"><p class="pi-label">Unit 3 · Session 8 · Complementary Grammar</p><h2>Your grammar goal</h2><p>Ask about a usual number of hours, offer an activity to try, and describe decided intentions with be going to.</p><div class="pi-route"><span>8 questions and answers about hours</span><span>8 suggestions with could try</span><span>8 intentions with going to</span></div><p class="pi-small">This practice was written for the course pacing guide. It is additional material; it is not an original exercise from the ESL Pals PDF. The PDF supports the Healthy Lifestyle theme. The schedules and people in these examples are fictional. The example hours do not set personal targets.</p><p class="pi-small">Complete an exercise before checking. Explanations and model audio appear after two different complete attempts, or after a perfect first attempt. Repeating equivalent answers does not add an attempt. Each of the three exercises keeps its own draft, reset and undo in this browser tab, including after a reload. This is practice only; no official grade or teacher submission is created.</p><p><a href="unit-3-healthy-living.html#hours-frequency">Review the Unit 3 explanation</a></p><p id="sr-storage-status" class="pi-small" role="status" hidden></p></section><div class="pi-audio-controls" aria-label="Grammar practice audio controls"><span>Audio speed</span><button type="button" data-sr-speed="0.75" aria-pressed="false">0.75×</button><button type="button" data-sr-speed="1" aria-pressed="true">1.0×</button><button type="button" data-sr-speed="1.25" aria-pressed="false">1.25×</button><button type="button" data-sr-stop>Stop audio</button><span id="sr-audio-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Listen to an instruction, worked example or underlined expression.</span></div>'''
